# epic_client.py's SMART Backend Services private key(s) — never
# committed. The matching *public* key lives in epic/jwks.json, which IS
# committed (see scripts/generate_epic_jwks.py) — the JWKS is meant to be
# hosted from this GitHub project so Epic's authorization server can
# fetch it, but the private key that signs client-assertion JWTs must
# never leave local/deployment-secret storage.
*.pem
/epic_private_key*
